{{!--
	link-mage-focus-as-items — one Focus pick (Paradigm / Practice / Instrument): a name and the
	eye icon that opens the item's own read-only `ItemViewer` in a SEPARATE WINDOW.

	SUPERSEDES the `<details>`/`<summary>` in-place disclosure this partial shipped with
	originally (design D3, `link-mage-focus-as-items`). That version was written against a stale
	premise — that "the same mechanics as a merit row" still named an inline reveal — recorded and
	corrected in D3's "Amended after implementation" note. The user asked afterwards for the
	gesture to actually match: every other row on this sheet (merits, flaws, backgrounds,
	abilities, spheres) opens the eye-icon `ItemViewer`, and a Focus row expanding in place while
	everything else opens a window was the inconsistency this follow-up removes.

	NOT `feature_item.hbs`. That partial is shared by twelve blocks across three tabs and carries a
	drag handle, an `isactive` checkbox, rollable dice/difficulty columns and a point-value column —
	a Focus pick has none of those, and suppressing four things with flags in a partial that busy
	would put its other twelve callers at risk for this one caller's shape. Still true, and still
	the reason this stays a dedicated partial rather than becoming a thirteenth caller.

	What this row now reuses IS the merit rows' own mechanism, verbatim: the eye icon markup
	(`.collapsible.button[data-itemid]`, no `data-action` of its own) that `feature_item.hbs`
	dropped and `stats_feature_row.hbs` still carries, bound once per render by
	`_bindCollapsibleButtons` (pc-actor-sheet.js) to `_handleCollapsibleClick`, which resolves
	`data-itemid` through `this.actor.items.get()` and calls `ItemViewer.open(item)` — the exact
	same read-only window every other row's eye opens. No new binder, no new selector:
	`.collapsible.button[data-itemid]` is already hard-coded in `pc-actor-sheet.js` and already
	checked by `binder-selector-check.py` against whatever markup in this sheet's template closure
	can produce it; this row simply becomes one more producer.

	The description is therefore no longer resolved for THIS row at all — `ItemViewer#_prepareContext`
	(item-viewer.js) resolves it live from the compendium through the item's own provenance, the
	SAME `resolveDescription` call this row used to make through `enrichFocusItems`
	(pc-actor-sheet.js). That function (and the `enrichedDescription`/`hasDescription` properties it
	set on each item) is dead now that nothing reads them, and is removed rather than left behind —
	verified by rendering a mage's Focus rows and opening the viewer, not by inspection alone.

	`data-itemid` is stamped on the row AND on the eye icon: the row's copy is what the offline
	orphan sweep (`test-part-render.mjs`) uses as evidence that a SPECIFIC item (not merely its
	block) reached the page, and the icon's copy is what the click handler actually reads.
--}}
<div class="v3-focusitem" data-itemid="{{item._id}}">
	<span class="v3-focuslabel splatFont" title="{{item.name}}">{{item.name}}</span>
	<i class="pullRight pointer icon collapsible button fa-solid fa-eye"
		title="{{localize 'wod.labels.show.description'}}"
		data-itemid="{{item._id}}"></i>
</div>
